FlyBlind TOP-UP plan (13 runs, 3 series) -- THROWAWAY: these conditions are also in campaign.sh

Runs only what was added after the first 52-run campaign, so the existing results are not repeated.
Same requirements as the full campaign: an active graphical session (every run opens QGroundControl,
no screen lock / suspend during ~4 h) and the FULL sidecar profile on every run.

  X1_core_extra  10 runs  ./start_testbed.sh                (default: co-located victim, 106 PRB, UL patch armed)
                          video onset at the predicted share (6 Mb x3)
                          | video plateau above the share (16 Mb x3, 24 Mb x3)
                          | one 106 PRB capacity replicate (24 Mb x1, expected invalid)
  X3_prb51_extra  2 runs  GNB_PRB=51 ./start_testbed.sh     51 PRB capacity lower bound (16 Mb x2) -- the first
                          campaign got 0 valid here, leaving C(51) with no floor
  X6_poscontrol   1 run   ./start_testbed.sh                positive control: the command leg is blackholed in
                          steady flight for longer than FS_GCS_TIMEOUT, so the native failsafe MUST trip
                          (GUIDED->RTL) -- expected invalid by construction, read as a control

What the two video groups test (one model, two sides of the same boundary, AoI = (Q/C)(N+1)):
  onset   -- measured UL capacity C ~= 24..32 Mb/s, so the share at N=4 is C/5 ~= 4.8..6.4 Mb/s. The attack is
             absent at 4 Mb/s and present at 8 Mb/s, so 6 Mb/s sits on the predicted boundary.
  plateau -- above the share the age is set by the buffer drained at the share, so it must NOT grow with the
             victim's offered rate: 16 and 24 Mb/s must reproduce the 12 Mb/s headline (~13 s).

N=5/N=6 is NOT included: start_testbed.sh accepts rogues=1..4 and only four rogue subscribers are provisioned,
so more co-tenants would require changing the testbed. The model is probed along the victim's demand instead.

Estimated wall time: ~4 h (13 x ~16 min + 3 bring-ups).
